    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: expose `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans (country code, space, national digits grouped in threes, e.g. `+61 412 345 678`) \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec and mapped by MapStruct, I followed the existing derived-field pattern (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, `ageBand`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` getter. It reuses the model's existing `countryCodeOf(...)` (the single source of truth for splitting E.164 into country code + national number), then renders `+<cc>` followed by the national digits grouped in threes from the left. Returns `null` when there's no telephone and the raw value unchanged when no recognized country code is present.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field. MapStruct auto-maps it by name from `Owner.getTelephoneDisplay()` (no explicit `@Mapping` needed, consistent with `membershipLevel`, `getRegion`, etc.).\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` posts `0412 345 678` (normalized to `+61412345678`) and asserts `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`. Full `mvn test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures.",
